es 812 for 804. Still missing: the unit types' speed on a ground (PLAN 3.3b), org lost to damage, and 3.4 to 3.6 as before. 2026-10-06 (PLAN 3.3b, ADR-138; PLAN 3.3 done): terrain on the march. A template crosses a cell at the least `terrainMods.speed` of its manoeuvre elements for that ground, × the pace its mobility class's move cost gives: a heavy panzer division a marsh at 0.2 of its pace on plains (0.7 ÷ 3.5; 0.286 before), and the panzer division of 1938 a marsh and mountains at the 0.6 of its motorised infantry; a forest at half, as before (`tests/unit/terrainMarch.test.ts`). Still missing: the route by a template's own figures, org lost to damage, and 3.4 to 3.6 as before. 2026-10-06 (PLAN 3.4a, ADR-139): combined arms, the first of four rules of a table (SPEC §6.1). A side of a battle with infantry, artillery and armour alive in it fires × 1.15 (`data/combat.json`): the panzer division of 1938 takes 3,363 men from a holding infantry division on plains in 48 hours for 2,921 before, a tank brigade, which has no guns, 1,382 (`tests/unit/combinedArms.test.ts`). Still missing: the screen of infantry for armour on close ground, artillery against AT guns, armour against infantry in the open and the matrix (PLAN 3.4b to 3.4d), nothing of it on the page, and 3.5, 3.6 as before. 2026-10-06 (PLAN 3.4b, ADR-140): the second rule, the screen. A tank on forest or urban ground whose side has no infantry alive in the battle takes × 1.3 from every volley (`data/combat.json`; `tests/unit/combinedArms.test.ts`: the tanks of a brigade whose two infantry companies are destroyed, against the same with a rifle brigade beside it; × 1 on plains and hills, and for guns). Every template with tanks has infantry of its own, so it bites once that is dead: in the first year of seed 99, 34,160 volleys at 3 tank brigades, of 39,920 at armour on close ground. Still missing: artillery against AT guns, armour against infantry in the open and the matrix (PLAN 3.4c, 3.4d), nothing of it on the 